      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "622493a7966ab703c5d14624",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think there are three possible options for the behavior of the branch part.\n1. Each branch is calculated assuming that root can rotate, but root itself does not. (Fully compatible with Dynamic Bone.)\n2. Calculate each branch as if root can rotate, and rotate root itself (use average or representative because the rotation of each branch may be different)\n3. The branch part is completely fixed. (Current behavior of PhysBone)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
